---
export const prerender = true;

const effectiveDate = '26 November 2026';
const appName = 'Tsundoku';
const domainHost = 'tsundoku.singbaobao.com';
const contactEmail = 'test@beetlskills.com';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Terms of Service — {appName}</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light dark;
        --bg: #fafafa;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --text: #18181b;
        --muted: #52525b;
        --border: #e4e4e7;
        --accent: #0f766e;
      }

      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          --bg: #09090b;
          --surface: #111114;
          --text: #f4f4f5;
          --muted: #a1a1aa;
          --border: #27272a;
          --accent: #2dd4bf;
        }
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.65;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
      }

      main {
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: 3rem auto;
        padding: 2.25rem;
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 10px;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        font-size: 1.85rem;
        line-height: 1.25;
      }

      .meta {
        margin: 0 0 2rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
      }

      h2 {
        margin: 2rem 0 0.65rem;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
      }

      p,
      ul {
        margin: 0.6rem 0;
      }

      ul {
        padding-left: 1.4rem;
      }

      li + li {
        margin-top: 0.35rem;
      }

      a {
        color: var(--accent);
        text-underline-offset: 2px;
      }

      footer {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        padding-top: 1.25rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="meta">
        Application: <strong>{appName}</strong> ({domainHost}) &middot; Effective Date: {effectiveDate}
      </p>

      <p>
        These Terms of Service (&ldquo;Terms&rdquo;) govern your access to and use of{' '}
        <strong>{appName}</strong> at <a href={`https://${domainHost}`}>https://{domainHost}</a>.
        By using the service, you agree to these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Service Description</h2>
      <p>
        {appName} is a book catalog and shelf-tracking web application that allows users to scan or
        enter ISBNs, look up book metadata, and sync shelf records with Google Sheets and linked
        shelf views.
      </p>

      <h2>2. User Accounts and Google Integration</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You are responsible for maintaining the security of your sign-in session and account
          access.
        </li>
        <li>
          Connecting a Google Account grants {appName} permission only within the OAuth scopes you
          approve (such as accessing Google Sheets files you select or create for your shelves).
        </li>
        <li>
          You remain the owner of your Google Drive files and spreadsheet data, and you may revoke
          Google access at any time via your Google Account permissions.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Do not misuse, disrupt, or attempt unauthorized access to the application, its APIs, or
          underlying infrastructure.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not upload unlawful, infringing, or harmful content or use the service in violation of
          applicable laws or third-party service terms (including Google terms).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Availability and No Warranty</h2>
      <p>
        {appName} is provided on an &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo; basis.
        Features, integrations, and availability may change, pause, or be discontinued without prior
        notice, and third-party services (such as Google Drive, Google Sheets, and external book
        metadata APIs) may experience outages or rate limits outside our control.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, neither {appName} nor its operator is liable for any
        indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of data,
        spreadsheet rows, or service interruption resulting from your use of the application. Keep
        backups of important spreadsheet data.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. Changes take effect when published on this page
        with an updated effective date.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about these Terms, contact{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <footer>
        <a href="/">Back to {appName}</a> &middot; <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>